so it is a pick from Language: Other at +40 (90%), the note naming the language (a per_level 0 on a language group is refused by regression). Math: Basic is Mathematics: Basic. Tracking (humanoids) is Tracking (people); Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals. W.P. Archery and Targeting is W.P. Archery, as other classes store it. The two Wilderness picks take +15%; the two W.P. picks are any W.P. || HAND TO HAND: Expert granted; Martial Arts or Assassin cost one related pick and Commando two (the book''s or other is not stored). || RELATED: eight at level one and one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 13. Espionage excludes Forgery and Disguise (+5%), Medical is First Aid only (+5%), Military +10%, Rogue +5% except Computer Hacking, Science is Advanced Math and Astronomy only, Technical +5% except Computer Programming (the +5% read as the category''s, printed after the exception), Wilderness +5%, W.P. any except Sharpshooting. Pilot excludes robots, power armor, tanks and APCs and every aircraft and spacecraft row by name and prefix, the same exclusion the Rulian Translator stores. Cowboy, Electrical and Mechanical are none and not listed. Secondary: four at level one and one at levels 2, 4, 7, 10 and 14 from the same list without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: catalog rows by slug; satchel is purse-satchel and communicator is walkie-talkie, as other classes store them. The medium body armor, the weapon per W.P. with six clips, and the double-bladed Vibro-Spear are prose: the double spear (printed 90, 3D6 M.D., +1 parry and disarm, +1 strike when thrown, no price) is a special ability, not a gear row. || MONEY: player characters 2D4x100 credits; slaves none, a restriction line. || NOT STORED: height, weight, life span, habitat, slave market value (30,000-50,000 credits), allies and enemies are in the body."
