## Lore

The Staphra are a humanoid race from an ancient world, gifted with psionics, physical prowess and a little magic. Their females are strong, fast and enduring hunter-warriors; the frailer males are the healers, armorers, teachers, advisors, mages and spiritual leaders. Enslaved by the Splugorth a century ago, they accepted it more easily than most, because their own caste system allowed a slave to rise through hard work. Most Staphra now work to earn full Minion status, and the Kittani speak well of them. A final Bio-Wizard augmentation for the best female warriors is held in reserve until that status comes. They keep their old traditions, monthly gatherings among them, and their traditional double spear, now fitted with Vibro-Blades.

Every Staphra warrior is female. Trained in combat from birth, she is expected to have mastered the fighting arts by 10, to have proven herself as hunter and fighter by 13, and to be ready to mate by 16. Staphra Warriors are aggressive, quick to take offense and quick to act, stern, demanding and well organized, ruthless in battle, and excellent at strategy and tactics. A renegade player character is a no-nonsense, by-the-book soldier who trusts no one at first, but can come to real camaraderie with patient companions.

## Body

Grey-green to dark green, hairless but for a mane of black or dark red hair (females usually braid it), with red, orange or yellow eyes, a dark red pupil, and large slit nostrils that give the race its keen sense of smell. Females stand 7 to 8 feet (2.1 to 2.4 m) and weigh 350 to 500 lbs (157.5 to 225 kg), lean and sculpted rather than bulky. Average life span 70 years. Females outnumber males five to one.

## GM Notes

Habitat: wherever the Splugorth are; natively forests and grasslands. Slave Market Value: still classed as a slave race, so only rogues, renegades and the disobedient are sold, typically 30,000-50,000 credits and sometimes twice that. Allies: the Staphra count themselves allies of the Minions of Splugorth; the Kittani and the Altara Warrior Women respect them as near equals, and full Minion status is 3D4 years away. Enemies: every enemy of the Splugorth; renegades are treated as traitors by loyal Staphra.
